# Version follows semver; it becomes 1.0.0 (with date-released and the Zenodo DOI) when
# M6 is complete and v1.0.0 is tagged. See docs/release_checklist.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "neptune-fork: Le Verrier's 1846 prediction of Neptune, rebuilt as a calibrated Bayesian inference"
abstract: >-
  Rebuilds Le Verrier's 1846 inference of Neptune from Uranus's motion from first principles:
  an own Wisdom-Holman N-body integrator validated against REBOUND, Uranus's orbit always
  fitted jointly with an unseen perturber, partitioned nested sampling for multimodal
  posteriors and evidence, and coverage tests on synthetic data. Includes a double-entry
  transcription of Le Verrier's 1846 Table n. 77 (279 observations) and an apparent-place
  observation model with per-observer error calibration. So far, synthetic-data results
  only. Code is MIT; the data in data/historical/ are dedicated to the public domain under
  CC0 1.0.
authors:
